Sure! Below is a simple example of a CSS card that rotates when you hover over it. You can copy this code into an HTML file and open it in your browser to see the effect.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Example</title>
<style>
/* Container for the card */
.card-container {
  perspective: 1000px; /* Gives depth to the 3D transform */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fad0c4 100%);
  border-radius: 15px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease-in-out;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;
  position: relative;
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg); /* Rotates the card 180 degrees around the Y-axis */
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden; /* Hides the back side when facing away */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  color: white;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  border-radius: 15px;
}

/* Back side of the card */
.card .back {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #a18cd1 0%, #fbc2eb 100%);
  transform: rotateY(180deg); /* Rotates the back side so it's visible after flip */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-container">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front side -->
    <div class="front">Front Side</div>
    <!-- Back side -->
    <div class="back">Back Side</div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works
1. **Perspective**: The `.card-container` has `perspective: 1000px;` which gives the 3D effect depth.
2. **Transition**: The `.card` uses `transition: transform 0.6s ease-in-out;` for smooth animation.
3. **Hover**: On hover, the card rotates 180 degrees around the Y-axis.
4. **Backface Visibility**: `backface-visibility: hidden;` hides the backside when it's not facing the viewer.
5. **Front & Back**: Both sides are absolutely positioned and centered with flexbox.

Feel free to customize colors, text, or dimensions to fit your design. Let me know if you'd like to add more features or tweak anything else!
